# ─── Bliss ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Bliss works with NO configuration. The primary provider (CVRON FreeAiAPIs) is a
# public, key-less API, so there are no secrets you must set to run it.
#
# Optional: point Bliss at a mirror or self-hosted gateway for the same API
# surface (e.g. if cvron.alwaysdata.net is rate-limiting you).
# NEXT_PUBLIC_AI_API_HOST="https://cvron.alwaysdata.net"

# Optional: server-only alias, same meaning, only read in route handlers.
# BLESS_API_BASE="https://cvron.alwaysdata.net"

# ─── Fallback provider · Agnes AI (optional) ─────────────────────────────
# https://www.agnes-ai.com/en/docs  ·  keys: https://platform.agnes-ai.com
#
# When this key is present, Bliss automatically retries a failed chat or image
# request against Agnes AI, and unlocks three documented extras: image (vision)
# analysis of a pasted image URL, native multi-turn context instead of the
# flattened prompt digest the key-less endpoints need, and asynchronous video
# tasks (text / keyframe / reference) with browser-side status polling.
#
# The key is not required to *pick* an Agnes model in the UI — every picker shows
# all documented ids, and choosing one without a key returns a clear error instead
# of quietly answering from the key-less provider.
#
# SERVER-ONLY. It is read in route handlers and never sent to the browser or
# inlined into the client bundle. Leave it unset and Bliss behaves exactly as
# before — nothing is faked, the fallback is simply reported as "not configured".
# AGNES_API_KEY=""

# Optional: which documented Agnes model answers when Bliss falls back.
# Allowed: agnes-2.5-flash (default) | agnes-3.0-flash. Unknown values are ignored.
# AGNES_CHAT_MODEL="agnes-2.5-flash"

# Optional: image model used for generation and edits (default agnes-image-2.1-flash).
# Also accepted: agnes-image-2.0-flash | agnes-image-2.5-flash.
# AGNES_IMAGE_MODEL="agnes-image-2.1-flash"

# Optional: default Agnes video model for an async task (default agnes-video-2.5-flash).
# Also accepted: agnes-video-2.5 — the billed engine, which additionally takes a
# reference video and 1080P/1K/2K output. Users can override either in Video Studio.
# AGNES_VIDEO_MODEL="agnes-video-2.5-flash"

# Optional: point the fallback at a different gateway host (base must end in /v1).
# AGNES_BASE_URL="https://apihub.agnes-ai.com/v1"

# Optional: port for `npm run start`.
# PORT=3000
